homelab-certsync (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release. Consumer half of the fleet certificate pipeline: fetches
    this host's certificates from homelab-api's certificate store, decrypts
    them locally with the shared KEK, validates (not expired, chain is a real
    chain, key matches cert, hashes match what was published), installs
    atomically and reloads the service -- only when the bytes actually
    changed. Runs at boot ordered BEFORE nginx/postfix/dovecot so a
    long-powered-off standby never serves a stale certificate, and hourly
    after that. Fail-safe: an unreachable API can never block a service start.

 -- Gardner <gardner@homelab>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:40:00 -0500
